# Server Page Checklist

Every protected page follows this order:

```tsx
export const metadata: Metadata = { title: "Clients" }; // UI label, not entity name

export default async function MembersPage() {
  const user = await requireAuth();                            // 1. auth guard (redirects to /login)
  const profile = await getCurrentUserProfile(user.id);       // 2. profile
  await requireTrialAccess(profile.organizationId);           // 3. trial guard (redirects to /settings/billing)
  const data = await getSomeData();                           // 4. data fetch (only if all guards pass)

  return (
    <AppLayout>
      <PageHeader title="Clients" description="..." action={<Button>...</Button>} />
      <div className="container mx-auto px-4 py-6">
        <ClientContainer fallbackData={data} />               // 5. pass as fallbackData
      </div>
    </AppLayout>
  );
}
```

# Rules

- `requireAuth` from `@/lib/auth`, `requireTrialAccess` from `@/lib/trial-server`
- `getCurrentUserProfile` from `@/lib/supabase/queries` (wrapped in React `cache()` — safe to call multiple times)
- Owner-only pages (billing, plans): use `requireOwnerServer()` from `@/lib/api-permissions` and `redirect()` if null
- Wrap everything in `<AppLayout>` — it renders the sidebar and mobile nav
- Use `<PageHeader>` for page title + action button
- Export `metadata` with UI-friendly title (see UI Naming below)
- Do NOT add `loading.tsx` to pages with `await` in the component — use the SWR fallback pattern instead

# UI Naming (display labels vs code names)

| Code entity    | UI label     |
|----------------|--------------|
| members        | Clients      |
| visits         | Appointments |
| team/profiles  | Staff        |
| event_types    | Services     |
| event_categories | Categories |
